# KGM agent workspace

One local home for three kinds of agent assets:

```text
control/              safe maintenance tools
content/skills/       shared Skills
content/settings/     global rules, settings, and hooks
content/subagent/     persona/subagent source and imported definitions
state/                private local state, backups, and receipts (Git-ignored)
```

The installer preserved every replaced original as a timestamped sibling backup. It did not create a Git commit, remote, or public repository.

## Daily maintenance

- Add a Skill: `control/bin/new-skill.sh <name> "description"`
- Rebuild the index: `python3 -B control/bin/rebuild-claude-md.py`
- Validate Skills: `bash control/bin/validate-skills.sh`
- Repair missing links: `bash control/bin/link-local.sh`
- Use from Kimi: install `content/skills/kgm-kimi-agent-workspace-bridge` through Kimi's normal Skill installation flow

`link-local.sh` never imports or replaces an unexpected existing path. Inventory and migration belong to the `kgm-agent-workspace-bootstrap` Skill so they always use a reviewed plan digest.

If installation was interrupted by a crash or power loss, do not relink manually. Run the Skill's `scripts/scaffold.py --recover-root <this-folder>` command so it validates the private write-ahead journal and restores the original paths.

Claude Code, Codex, `.agents`, and Hermes use registered links. Kimi uses the generated read-only bridge Skill. It exposes Skill manifests, four shared rule documents, and Markdown persona/subagent files—not runtime configuration—and does not inspect or change `.kimi`.
